<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-6">
  <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Config",
    subtitle: "Set up your initializer after installation.",
    variant: :h1
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Steps",
      subtitle: "Follow these steps to configure the gem in your app.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Open <span class="font-mono">config/initializers/recording_studio_ai.rb</span>.</li>
      <li>Paste the initializer template below and adjust values for your environment.</li>
      <li>Add provider API keys and choose the profile/fallback strategy you want to support.</li>
      <li>Restart the app so initializer changes are loaded.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Initializer example",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @config_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "1. Add a Provider",
      subtitle: "Providers are single adapter classes (for example OpenAI and Gemini). Each provider is one class under lib/recording_studio_ai/providers/<provider>.rb.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Create a provider class under <span class="font-mono">lib/recording_studio_ai/providers/&lt;provider&gt;.rb</span> that inherits <span class="font-mono">RecordingStudioAI::Providers::Base</span> and declares <span class="font-mono">provider_key</span>.</li>
      <li>Implement the contract methods your models need: <span class="font-mono">generate</span>, <span class="font-mono">stream</span>, and the batch methods.</li>
      <li>Register it from the host initializer or another gem's engine initializer with <span class="font-mono">RecordingStudioAI.register_provider(:key, instance)</span>.</li>
      <li>Optionally set <span class="font-mono">config.discovery_enabled = true</span> to auto-register provider classes found under the providers path.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Provider registration examples",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @provider_extension_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "2. Add a Model",
      subtitle: "Models are declarative registration scripts (no class). Built-ins ship with the gem; add your own the same way.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Pick the provider the model belongs to (it must be registered first).</li>
      <li>Create a registration file. For gem-style catalogs use <span class="font-mono">lib/recording_studio_ai/models/&lt;provider-key&gt;/&lt;model-key&gt;.rb</span> (for example <span class="font-mono">models/openai/gpt-5-mini.rb</span>, <span class="font-mono">models/gemini/gemini-2-5-pro.rb</span>). For a host app, any initializer works.</li>
      <li>The file/key is a lowercase hyphenated slug (dots become hyphens); the <span class="font-mono">model:</span> value is the exact provider API model string used in profiles.</li>
      <li>Call <span class="font-mono">RecordingStudioAI.models.register(...)</span> and declare <span class="font-mono">delivery</span>, <span class="font-mono">parameters</span>, <span class="font-mono">tools</span>, and <span class="font-mono">modalities</span> so the resolver and AI playground know what the model supports.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Model registration",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @model_registration_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "3. Create Profiles",
      subtitle: "Profiles are ordered preference lists of provider/model candidates used by generate, stream, and batch.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Set <span class="font-mono">config.profiles</span> in <span class="font-mono">config/initializers/recording_studio_ai.rb</span>.</li>
      <li>Reference each model by its provider API model string (the <span class="font-mono">model:</span> value from registration). Do not repeat capabilities here — they come from the model registry.</li>
      <li>Order candidates by preference; the resolver picks the first configured provider whose model supports the request.</li>
      <li>Set <span class="font-mono">config.default_profile</span> and, optionally, <span class="font-mono">config.profile_fallbacks</span> for tier fallback.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Profile configuration",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @profile_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Create Custom Tools",
      subtitle: "Register a tool and call it from generate/stream requests.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6">
      <li>Define a stable key and version for your tool.</li>
      <li>Provide clear parameter schema and usage guidance.</li>
      <li>Implement a deterministic executor that returns serializable data.</li>
      <li>Pass the tool reference in the request's custom_tools array.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    title: "Custom tool registration and usage",
    language: "ruby",
    code: @custom_tools_example
  ) %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Configuration Reference",
      subtitle: "Meaning, accepted values, and requirement level for each option.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="min-w-full text-left text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-(--surface-border-color)">
            <th class="px-2 py-2 font-semibold">Key</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-2 font-semibold">Required</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-2 font-semibold">Accepted values</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-2 font-semibold">Explanation</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% @config_options.each do |option| %>
            <tr class="border-b border-(--surface-border-color)">
              <td class="px-2 py-2 align-top font-mono text-xs"><%= option[:key] %></td>
              <td class="px-2 py-2 align-top"><%= option[:required] %></td>
              <td class="px-2 py-2 align-top"><%= option[:accepted_values] %></td>
              <td class="px-2 py-2 align-top"><%= option[:explanation] %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
